 "title": "Home electricity prices vs. the cost of making power",
 "unit": "dollars per MWh (divide by 10 for cents per kWh)",
 "notes": "Three measures of what electricity costs before it reaches your home, compared with what Virginia homes pay. Wholesale figures are averages for the whole PJM region (13 states and D.C., including Virginia), per MWh of load, before local distribution. The Virginia fleet figure covers fuel plus operation and maintenance for power plants located in Virginia; it leaves out the cost of building them. None of the figures are adjusted for inflation.",
